{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XWzshzgJhCAKJiX7SA2dR3","type":"tool_result","content":"depth 2; vs CooperateBot D, vs DefectBot D, vs FairBot C (FairBot replies C), vs itself C; prudent: YES\n2026-10-22T22:00:34Z [opus] Agree with sol's depth-1 proof (I derived the same). Depth-2 prudent agent verified by check.py: B(a & (B(F) | ~d)) (= PrudentBot, □(a ∧ (¬□⊥→¬d))). Also B(a) & B(~B(F) -> ~d). I'm writing answer.md now with DEPTH: 2 + proof; will look at minimal size for Q3. Others: please don't overwrite, append comments instead.\n2026-10-22T22:00:34Z [sol] FOUND depth-2 prudent candidate: B(a) & (B(B(F)) | ~B(d)). Checker next. Mechanism: CB C at n0,1 then D; DB C at n0 then D; FB/self always C. Together with my unrestricted depth-1 lower bound this solves required parts. I will write answer.md shortly unless another agent has draft ownership.\n2026-10-22T22:00:42Z [sol] Opus: your candidate is shorter (8 syntax-tree symbols counting each connective, box, atom, constant once) than mine (10). Agree you own answer.md; I will independently verify your candidate and inspect proof, not overwrite. Your candidate yields same traces CB C,C,D..., DB C,D..., FB/self C forever.\n2026-10-22T22:00:57Z [argon] Starting analysis of world-by-world valuation sequences v_Y(n) = (a,c,d) for Y in {CB, DB, FB, X}.\n2026-10-22T22:01:00Z [sol] Independently verified opus formula using reference checker: depth 2, D,D,C,C, FairBot replies C, prudent YES. Rigorous trace proof: outer box vacuous at n0; X-DB D from n1 since a=false at m0. Then FB's d and self's d each equal C only at m0, where B(F) masks them. Both a streams stay all C inductively, hence mutual/self cooperation. CB fails at m1 and so X-CB D from n2. Ready to review answer and finalize; success rules say stop when required formula+lower-bound proof are complete.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d1146e5c-84be-4d08-bc92-04d94440795d","uuid":"435c84d1-beae-4